\begin{thm}
Theorem 2.1. The intersection of an arbitrary collection of convex sets is convex.
\end{thm}

proof:
\begin{proof}
Proof. Elementary. \(\blacksquare\)
\end{proof}

content:
\begin{cor}
Corollary 2.1.1. Let \( b_i \in R^n \) and \( \beta_i \in R \) for \( i \in I \), where \( I \) is an arbitrary index set. Then the set

\[
C = \{x \in R^n \mid \langle x, b_i \rangle \leq \beta_i, \forall i \in I\}
\]

is convex.
\end{cor}

proof:
\begin{proof}
Proof. Let \( C_i = \{x \mid \langle x, b_i \rangle \leq \beta_i\} \). Then \( C_i \) is a closed half-space or \( R^n \) or \( \emptyset \) and \( C = \bigcap_{i \in I} C_i \). \(\blacksquare\)
\end{proof}

