\begin{thm}
Theorem 3.3. Let \(\{C_i \mid i \in I\}\) be an arbitrary collection of non-empty convex sets in \(R^n\), and let \(C\) be the convex hull of the union of the collection. Then

\[ C = \bigcup \{\sum_{i \in I} \lambda_i C_i\}, \]

where the union is taken over all finite convex combinations (i.e. over all non-negative choices of the coefficients \(\lambda_i\) such that only finitely many are non-zero and these add up to 1).
\end{thm}

\begin{thm}
Theorem 3.4. Let \( A \) be a linear transformation from \( R^n \) to \( R^m \). Then \( AC \) is a convex set in \( R^m \) for every convex set \( C \) in \( R^n \), and \( A^{-1}D \) is a convex set in \( R^n \) for every convex set \( D \) in \( R^m \).
\end{thm}

proof:
