content:
\begin{cor}
Corollary 3.4.1. The orthogonal projection of a convex set \( C \) on a subspace \( L \) is another convex set.
\end{cor}

proof:
\begin{proof}
Proof. The orthogonal projection mapping onto \( L \) is a linear transformation, the one which assigns to each point \( x \) the unique \( y \in L \) such that \( (x - y) \perp L \). \(\|\)
\end{proof}

