Theorem 3.5. Let \( C \) and \( D \) be convex sets in \( R^m \) and \( R^n \), respectively. Then

\[
C \oplus D = \{ x = (y, z) \mid y \in C, z \in D \}
\]

is a convex set in \( R^{m+p} \).
\end{thm}

