\begin{thm}
Theorem 4.7. A positively homogeneous function \(f\) from \(R^n\) to \((-\infty, +\infty]\) is convex if and only if

\[ f(x + y) \leq f(x) + f(y) \]

for every \(x \in R^n\), \(y \in R^n\).
\end{thm}

proof:
\begin{proof}
Proof. This is implied by Theorem 2.6, because the subadditivity condition on \(f\) is equivalent to \(\text{epi} f\) being closed under addition. \(\|\)
\end{proof}

content:
\begin{cor}
Corollary 4.7.1. If \(f\) is a positively homogeneous proper convex function, then

\[ f(\lambda_1 x_1 + \cdots + \lambda_m x_m) \leq \lambda_1 f(x_1) + \cdots + \lambda_m f(x_m) \]

whenever \(\lambda_1 > 0, \ldots, \lambda_m > 0\).
\end{cor}

\begin{cor}
Corollary 4.7.2. If \(f\) is a positively homogeneous proper convex function, then \(f(-x) \geq -f(x)\) for every \(x\).
\end{cor}

proof:
\begin{proof}
Proof. \(f(x) + f(-x) \geq f(x - x) = f(0) \geq 0\). \(\|\)
\end{proof}

